{"findings":[{"file":"black.py","line":222,"what_goes_wrong":"`find_pyproject_toml()` passes its documented string path directly to an iterable-of-paths function, so the path is processed character by character and configuration discovery can crash.","trigger":"Call `find_pyproject_toml()` with a Windows path to a directory containing `pyproject.toml`, such as `C:\\...\\tmpdir`.","expected":"It should return that directory's `pyproject.toml` path.","actual":"It raises `OSError: [WinError 123]` while trying to resolve the `:` character as a path component.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport black\n\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n    root = Path(directory)\n    expected = root / \"pyproject.toml\"\n    expected.write_text(\"[tool.black]\\n\", encoding=\"utf8\")\n    assert black.find_pyproject_toml(str(root)) == str(expected)\n"},{"file":"black.py","line":4123,"what_goes_wrong":"An empty cache file is not treated as malformed even though `read_cache()` promises to ignore malformed caches.","trigger":"The formatter cache file exists but is zero bytes, for example after an interrupted cache write.","expected":"It should return an empty cache and continue formatting.","actual":"`pickle.load()` raises `EOFError`, causing formatting to fail.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport black\n\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n    black.CACHE_DIR = Path(directory)\n    black.get_cache_file(black.Mode()).write_bytes(b\"\")\n    assert black.read_cache(black.Mode()) == {}\n"},{"file":"blackd.py","line":163,"what_goes_wrong":"An empty `X-Python-Variant` header causes an uncaught `IndexError` instead of being rejected as an invalid header.","trigger":"Send blackd a request with `X-Python-Variant: ` (an empty value).","expected":"The parser should raise `InvalidVariantHeader`, allowing the handle